{"name":"Lira","hex":"#e2c28d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lira","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Spanish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lira"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lira","blocks":[{"text":"Lira is the name of several currency units. It is the current currency of Turkey and also the local name of the currencies of Lebanon and of Syria. It is also the name of several former currencies, including those of Italy, Malta and Israel. The term originates from the value of a Roman pound of high purity silver. The libra was the basis of the monetary system of the Roman Empire. When Europe resumed a monetary system, during the Carolingian Empire, the Roman system was adopted. The Roman denominations librae, solidi, denarii were used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/100_Lira_%28Italy%29.jpg/330px-100_Lira_%28Italy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lira","wikidata":"Q7995739"},{"title":"Lira (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Lerato Moipone Molapo, known professionally as Lira, is a South African singer. Her name translates to \"love\" in Sesotho and she speaks four languages. She is a multi-platinum selling and an 11-time South African Music Award (SAMA)-winning Afro-soul vocalist, who refers to her music as \"a fusion of soul, funk, elements of jazz and African.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Lira_%28South_African_singer%29.jpg/330px-Lira_%28South_African_singer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lira_(singer)","wikidata":"Q3644160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Lira_coin.png/500px-Lira_coin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Lira_coin.png/500px-Lira_coin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALira_coin.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/VE2_lira_1863.jpg/500px-VE2_lira_1863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/VE2_lira_1863.jpg/500px-VE2_lira_1863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVE2_lira_1863.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/10_Lira_%28Turkey%29.jpg/500px-10_Lira_%28Turkey%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/10_Lira_%28Turkey%29.jpg/1280px-10_Lira_%28Turkey%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/10_Lira_%28Turkey%29.jpg/500px-10_Lira_%28Turkey%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A10_Lira_(Turkey).jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}